  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Four identical long solenoids <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></math>&nbsp;are connected to each other as shown in the figure. If the magnetic field at the center of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math> the field at the center of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> would be : (Assume that the magnetic field is confined with in the volume of respective solenoid).</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0147_108db0c19786.png\" style=\"width: 373px; height: 165px;\" /></p>"
